namespace Survsys.Data;

/// <summary>
/// The rows <see cref="CodeValueConfiguration"/> seeds <c>code_values</c> with:
/// every reference list a coded field is chosen from.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
/// Generated from the legacy Flyway seed under
/// <c>../nedss/legacy/nedss-jpa/src/main/resources/db/migration</c>, one list
/// per legacy reference table: <c>V0003__init.sql</c> for most of them,
/// <c>V0009__more_init_source_type.sql</c> for source type,
/// <c>V0158__add_cntry_usual_res_and_more.sql</c> for transmission mode,
/// <c>V0164__redefine_countries.sql</c> for country,
/// <c>V0169__create_vaccine_tables.sql</c> for the vaccine manufacturer and
/// information source, and <c>V0221__add_residence_types.sql</c> for residence
/// type. The legacy test type and organism tables have no code, only a name,
/// so the name is the code and there is no description. A legacy table with no
/// sort order is kept in the order the seed inserts it. A code the legacy
/// inserts twice in different case (contact type <c>INFANT</c> and
/// <c>infant</c>) is kept once, as first inserted, because codes here compare
/// without case.
///
/// Three lists have no legacy table: task priority and encounter type are the
/// fixed options the legacy task and encounter screens offer, and the
/// attachment categories are the ones the legacy upload dialog offers.
///
/// The county list is Utah's legacy codes and, after them, Connecticut's
/// historical counties and planning regions, which no legacy table holds; each
/// county row carries its state, its FIPS code where it has one, and its kind.
///
/// Each row's <see cref="CodeValue.Id"/> is fixed here, in this order, so a
/// coded field that holds an id names the same code in every environment.
/// </remarks>
